=== (2) conformal time of a closed de Sitter phase ===
  d eta/dt - 1/R(t) = 0
  eta(t -> oo) = pi/2
  5 e-folds after the throat: eta_end = 1.564058328811049 (pi/2 = 1.570796326794897)
  50 e-folds after the throat: eta_end = 1.570796326794897 (pi/2 = 1.570796326794897)
  60 e-folds after the throat: eta_end = 1.570796326794897 (pi/2 = 1.570796326794897)
  start at R_i = 1 c/H: eta added = 1.570796; arcsin(c/(H R_i)) = 1.570796
  start at R_i = 2 c/H: eta added = 0.523599; arcsin(c/(H R_i)) = 0.523599
  start at R_i = 10 c/H: eta added = 0.100167; arcsin(c/(H R_i)) = 0.100167
  start at R_i = 1000.0 c/H: eta added = 0.001000; arcsin(c/(H R_i)) = 0.001000

=== (3) light that starts at an inflationary throat (dust-cycloid approximation after inflation) ===
  radiation bang (dynamics convention): antipode at eta_post = 3.1416 -> a/a_max = 1.000, t/t_turn = 1.000;  full circuit at eta_post = 6.2832 -> a/a_max = 0.000 (collapse), t/t_turn = 2.000
  throat start: antipode at eta_post = 1.5708 -> a/a_max = 0.500, t/t_turn = 0.182;  full circuit at eta_post = 4.7124 -> a/a_max = 0.500 (collapse), t/t_turn = 1.818
  (radiation-bang values in the dynamics grid: antipode at t/t_turn = 0.76-0.998, circuit near the crunch, phase-dependent; the throat start adds pi/2 and moves both well away from the turnaround and the crunch)
